+---
+id: task-004-fix-coupon-stacking-order-and-inclusive-coupon-expiry-clarify-shipping-vat-is-by-design
+type: task
+title: "fix coupon stacking order and inclusive coupon expiry; clarify shipping VAT is by design"
+status: pending
+---
+
+Three reports came in about the order service. Handled each against the business rules in
+`README.md`.
+
+## 1. Finance: volume discount + percentage coupon gives too much off
+
+12 notebooks at €5.00 with a 10% coupon priced to €48.00 of goods instead of the expected €48.60.
+
+Cause: `priceOrder` in `src/pricing.ts` computed the coupon's percentage on the order's gross total,
+before the volume discount, instead of on the subtotal after volume discounts as the README requires
+("a coupon ... applies to the order's subtotal after volume discounts"). For the example: gross
+€60.00, volume discount €6.00 (10% of €60.00), coupon wrongly taken as 10% of €60.00 = €6.00 instead
+of 10% of €54.00 = €5.40, giving €48.00 instead of €48.60.
+
+Fix: `couponDiscount` is now computed on `grossTotal - volumeTotal` (the post-volume-discount
+subtotal) rather than on `grossTotal`. The 50%-of-gross cap in `capped()` is unchanged, since that cap
+is explicitly on the gross amount.
+
+Test added: `test/coupons.test.ts` — "applies a percentage coupon to the subtotal after volume
+discount, not before", reproducing the finance example (12 units, volume discount, percent coupon)
+and asserting goods come to 4860 cents.
+
+## 2. Customer (Luca): coupon AUTUMN, valid until 30 November, refused as expired on 30 November
+
+Cause: `Coupons.redeemable` in `src/coupons.ts` rejected a coupon when `date >= validUntil`, i.e. on
+the last valid day itself, contradicting the README ("valid from its first day to its last day, both
+included").
+
+Fix: changed the comparison to `date > validUntil` so the last day is accepted.
+
+Test added: `test/coupons.test.ts` — "is valid through its last day, inclusive", placing an order on
+a coupon's `validUntil` date and asserting the coupon discount applies.
+
+## 3. Customer (Anna): VAT charged on shipping (€1.08 on €4.90)
+
+Checked against the README: "Shipping is subject to VAT at the standard rate (22%), shown on its own
+line of the receipt." €4.90 × 22% = €1.078, rounded half up to €1.08 — exactly what Anna saw, and
+exactly what the documented business rule calls for. This is existing, already-tested behaviour
+(`test/orders.test.ts`, "prices a small order"), not a defect.
+
+No code change made for this report. Per the repository's rule that the README is authoritative when
+it and the code disagree, charging VAT on shipping is correct as specified; changing it would require
+a product/business decision to amend the VAT rule itself, which is out of scope for a bug fix and not
+something to decide unilaterally.
+
+## Verification
+
+`npm test` — 19/19 passing (2 new tests were red before the pricing.ts/coupons.ts fixes, green after).
